of the solution, bringing the equilibrium pH closer to neutral. This phenomenon can
potentially be ascribed to the fact that calcium alginate is a salt formed from a strong
base and a weak acid, coupled with the inherently alkaline physicochemical properties of
biochar. Whether the effect of Cd adsorption and raising pH of MB-CA are also excellent in

