2.3. The Effect of pH on the Adsorption of Cd2+ by MB-CA
Five 50 mL portions of Cd(NO3 )2 solution at a concentration of 50 mg/L were prepared
and the pH of each solution was adjusted to 2, 3, 4, 5 and 6, respectively. Subsequently,
0.06 g of MB-CA was added to each solution. The solutions were then magnetically agitated
at room temperature (25 ± 1) ◦ C for a duration of 24 h. Afterward, the concentrations of
Cd2+ in the solutions as well as their respective pH values were measured. A total of 3 sets
of parallel experiments were conducted and the results were averaged.

